{
 "name": "amd_stack12061",
 "description": "Stack #12059..#12061 (tip vs main) on gfx1151: the stock amd_strix_small cells plus DEFAULT-tier variants, because the stack's ROCm-reachable changes (one-frame Qwen-Image 2D VAE, Qwen-Image-2.1 VAE contiguous + cudnn skip, HV1.5 mask) are all skipped on speed_mode off. Small models on the AMD Strix Halo gfx1151 CI (Radeon 8060S, 64 GiB unified, ROCm 7.13 torch 2.11 from repo.amd.com/rocm/whl/gfx1151). Run by amd/diffusion_probe.py once per state (base / head), in the Studio venv the job installed (Linux) or the venv the probe builds (Windows). Studio never compiles on ROCm (inductor _alloc_from_pool fails for every arm), so speed_mode default is eager there and quant arms are native weight-only (PR 11631, no torchao on Windows). Tiers run in order: tiny_* first (hf-internal-testing random pipelines, 1 to 56 MB downloads, seconds per cell: plumbing only, judged on broken / newly flagged, never on pixels or timing), then the small real models (sdxlt_* zimg_* wan_*), which the probe selects by default; heavy_* cells are opt-in (--only 'heavy_*') because one Qwen-Image-2.1 1024 image costs 180-270 s warm and ~1000 s cold on this APU. Public, ungated weights only: the runner never gets an HF token.",
